betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAEvA.desc=Nuclear fusion is the next major step in your progression, and to accomplish it you will need a Fusion Reactor Mark I. You will unlock new materials across the next few tiers with fusion, making this a required multiblock. Europium is what you will need first to make it to ZPM.%n%nAt the same time, fusion can generate power for you, primarily via Helium Plasma in this first tier. The speed of the reactor can make for significant EU/t, but actually consuming this plasma fast enough at this early stage is difficult. You will have Large Plasma Turbines, which can use a 4A Dynamo Hatch. This might require a lot of spam compared to powergen setups you might be using, such as UCFE, vac nukes or other options. Later, you will unlock XL turbines and a fusion line for them. %n%nFor your first reactor, you will need a controller, 1-16 fluid input hatches, 1-16 fluid output hatches, and 16 LuV+ energy hatches. Each energy hatch has an energy capacity of 10M EU and draws up to 2048 EU/t.%n%nThat means you can do any fusion recipe with a start cost of 160M EU or less, and takes 32768 EU/t or less. Using more fluid hatches means you need less fusion casings. While this doesn't matter as much for the mk1 reactor, this principle helps tremendously with the higher reactor tiers.%n%n[note]You'll notice that there is an option to create a Compact Fusion Reactor MKI instead of the normal size. This is available as an option for every tier of Fusion Reactor. They are not required by any means, but they are demonstrably quicker if you're willing to spend extra resources.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.8PiGBrdnSHOVIA7tHinlOA.desc=Sometimes, basic automation isn't enough. We've heard you - we are now offering the §5§nAdvanced Routing Package§r to allow more complex automation of your components!%n%nThe Nanopart Splitter allows splitting, merging and filtering of your components between different colored VCI and VCO hatches. In the configuration GUI, you can define rules such as:%n- Merging any colors of your choice into one color%n- Evenly splitting inputs from one color into many output colors%n- Filtering specific components from one color to another%nand many more!%n%nWe have expanded the functionality of Nanopart Splitter rules with feedback from our customers to also include ease-of-use features such as:%n- Middle clicking item filters to set them to a custom rename%n- Wildcard input color if no input color is selected%n- Even distribution to output colors if multiple output colors are selected%n- Filtering items using their normal form rather than requiring the component wrapped form%n%nAdditionally, if you purchase the Premium Package, you gain access to the Nanochip Redstone Input hatch, allowing for fine-grained redstone control of your routing. Each redstone hatch has a "channel" setting, which can then be configured in a rule for it to use that specific hatch's redstone signal. The hatch can also be used on some other modules, like the Board module (sold separately).
betterquesting.quest.94ivNBMMTAC7qATq_uroGw.desc=We get it, this isn't the most exciting piece of the puzzle. However, the §5§nFundamentals Package§r is essential to the entire operation.%n%nAllowing things such as:%n- Part Preparation for your surface mounted devices%n- Wafer Cutting for your advanced silicon parts among others%n- Wire Tracing for all your fine wires%n- Superconductor Splitting for your most expensive circuits%n- Encasement Wrapping for all your mainframe needs%n- Board Immersion for the base of your circuits*%n%nOne key detail for operating your modules at maximum recommended efficiency is the input separation rule. Each module included in this and other packages offers an input separation toggle, allowing one of two operating methods:%n1. §4Disabled:§r§r Input components will be processed separately per color, outputting to the same colored VCO%n2. §2Enabled:§r Input components will be merged between colors, outputting to the color of the recipe's first input%n%n§oNote*: The Full-Board Immersion Device requires a proper setup to ensure fluid purity. Read the owner's manual (tooltip) to see how to properly utilize this module.§r
betterquesting.quest.FlFle6Z7TZSkgpJjPi4ucA.desc=Now that you have the core pieces of the NAC™ platform, it's time to decide what circuit you would like to make. The §5§nCrystal Package§r allows for the creation of Crystal Circuits much more efficiently than other methods. See the attached owner's manual for installation instructions.%n%n§oIf you purchase in the next 72 hours, this package is 50%% off! Please... make a NAC™ for crystal circuits, CALs aren't as good we promise...§r%n%n%n§n§lUltra-high Energy Etching Array Owner's Manual:§r%n%nThe NAC™ will track the most recent 100,000 circuits crafted, and can be calibrated to a specific circuit type by reaching a certain percentage of circuits of this type. Mainframes count as one circuit crafted, with each tier below it counting for half as much as the last. At 60%% (60,000) crystal circuits crafted, the NAC™ will become "fully calibrated" to crystal circuits.%n%nOnce that has been met, the Laser Source Hatch on the Etching Array will provide two bonuses:%n- The §nEU Cost§r will be divided by each amperage interval over 256A. Example - 1,024A will divide by 2, 4,096A will divide by 3, etc.%n- The §nRecipe Duration§r will be divided by (hatch tier - 9). Example - UIV will divide by 2, UMV will divide by 3, etc.
betterquesting.quest.NAUxWAKzTHifGrUSGPcb5w.desc=So you've chosen the §5§nWetware and Bioware Package§r for your newly purchased NAC™. A wise choice, as these are some of the most important circuits you will make. See the attached owner's manual for installation instructions.%n%n§oGet it while you can! A two-for-one deal on circuit lines!§r%n%n§n§lAccelerated Biological Coordinator Owner's Manual:§r%n%nThe NAC™ will track the most recent 100,000 circuits crafted, and can be calibrated to a specific circuit type by reaching a certain percentage of circuits of this type. Mainframes count as one circuit crafted, with each tier below it counting for half as much as the last. At 60%% (60,000) wetware circuits crafted, the NAC™ will become "fully calibrated" to wetware circuits, and the same applies to bioware circuits.%n%nDepending on which calibration has been achieved, the Biological Coordinator will provide one of two bonuses:%n- If fully calibrated to §nWetware§r, usage of Catalyst Medium is reduced to 50%%%n- If fully calibrated to §nBioware§r, usage of Catalyst Medium is reduced to zero
betterquesting.quest.c9yhGUSqSBKfUE-I0l_kbw.desc=You've gotten this far, you know the drill. You've made more circuits than you can count, but what if that isn't enough? It's time to stop scaling the old way, and start manufacturing like the late game engineer you are.%n%nThe Nanochip Assembly Complex isn't just a fancier CAL or Assembly Line - it is the core of your entire operation. For the low price of a small craft* for your machines to chew on, you can be the proud owner of the latest innovation in circuit crafting technology! %n%nFor detailed operation information, please consult the Owner's Manual included by clicking on the company logo in the UI of the multiblock.%n%n§oNote*: "Small craft" may not accurately reflect the state of your industrialization and the company holds no accountability or liability for professional mishaps like "that's way too much UHV Superconductor" or "we need to scale our HILEs yesterday"§r%n%n§oNAC™ sold as-is. Functionality available via separately crafted modules
betterquesting.quest.oyyde6hbRUOyVcAf7IP5HA.desc=You may have noticed that Optical Circuits the way you're used to in the CAL and Assembly Line are far more expensive than any other circuit line. The NAC™ has just the solution for you!%n%nWe are offering the new §5§nOptical Package§r, allowing for much more efficient production of your optical circuits! See the attached owner's manual for installation instructions.%n%n§oAn external review has been conducted and has found the company §nnot responsible§r§o for changes to other methods of producing optical circuits. The benefits of a NAC™ for optical circuits are merely coincidental.§r§r%n%n§l§nOptically Optimized Organizer Owner's Manual§r%n%nThe Optically Optimized Organizer requires two different grades of purified water to function. However, these are not just an extra running cost! Each grade of water 3 and above provides a bonus to the module's running stats:%n- Grade 3 (1000L/s): 0.8x Water Cost (applies to both)%n- Grade 4 (800L/s): 0.6x Water Cost (applies to both)%n- Grade 5 (800L/s): 0.9x Recipe Duration Modifier%n- Grade 6 (600L/s): 0.7x Recipe Duration Modifier%n- Grade 7 (600L/s): 0.9x Recipe EU Cost%n- Grade 8 (400L/s): 0.7x Recipe EU Cost%n%nWater is only consumed while the module is running. Similar water bonuses (such as Grade 5 + Grade 6) can be applied together.%n%nThe NAC™ will track the most recent 100,000 circuits crafted, and can be calibrated to a specific circuit type by reaching a certain percentage of circuits of this type. Mainframes count as one circuit crafted, with each tier below it counting for half as much as the last. At 60%% (60,000) optical circuits crafted, the NAC™ will become "fully calibrated" to optical circuits.%n%nOnce that has been met, the bonuses from each chosen water type are applied twice.%n%nOptical circuits created by the Assembly Matrix have a §550%%§r chance of being output in an unorganized form, requiring them to be routed back through the Optical Organizer.
betterquesting.quest.qirJLnNZT6Wmb7oQJ1IOLg.desc=You might be saying, "So I've just purchased this thing, now what?" We have just the solution for you!%n%nThe §5§nAssembling Package§r is the most important upgrade to the NAC™ platform, allowing for the creation of circuits with your processed components. This isn't just another assembler - it's the most important machine you'll ever own.%n%nProvide the Nanochip Assembly Matrix with a Vacuum Conveyor Input (sold separately) containing the necessary components, and all the circuits you have ever wanted will be yours!%n%n§oPower costs may be high. The NAC™ offers no guarantees on your existing power network.
betterquesting.quest.2rrP1wt_Qt2LlOqDppdjLQ.desc=Planck-Scale Circuits, the final circuits in the pack... for now. These MAX circuits are needed for high end UXV parts and the Stargate.%n%n[note]You will need your Quantum NAC to get started%n%nDid you know that Calabi-Yau Manifolds, despite being classified as a circuit internally, do not contribute to the calibration of a Special NAC. Planck-Scale Circuits do, however.[/note]%n%n[warn]Whoever told you these rumors is lying to you, these circuits will NEVER be removed... or will they?[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.3jUq4tkmRty9x5vvnqtD9w.desc=Computation has gone too far! We've gone too small! Why does it look so cool! These Calabi-Yau Manifolds are incomprehensible to the human mind!%nGood thing we have GREGOS to comprehend them for us!%n%nIn order to fully prepare them for circuitry, the Raw Manifold Bud will need to be taken out of the NAC for further processing.%n%n[note]The precursor to Calabi-Yau Manifolds, Raw Manifold Buds, are manufactured in the NAC and act as circuits for calibration bonuses, but do not count towards calibration progress.[/note]%n%n[warn]Do not put these in your mouth.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.uPmgcTcIR6OcAYqLCD7IkQ.desc=GregTech now makes &z&qice creams§r. Yes, really.%n%nSomewhere out there is a machine that turns... something... into ice cream. Lots of flavors. Some good, some weird, some questionable.%n%nGo find it and see what you get.%n%n[note]This machine does not use any power.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.b_Ll4zvSRfCMgmqiBa4Xkw.desc=It's easy to lose Ore Drilling Plants. You're a busy engineer, you know? You can't be bothered to remember trifling things like "where, in what galactic backwater did I last place my miner." You could do something boring like "write down the location of the miner" or "put up a sign with the miner's location in my ore processing area," but there's a better way.%n%nEnter the Metrics Transmitter Cover. This cover, when attached to a multiblock miner (or any GregTech machine), spawns in a GregTech Advanced Sensor Card paired to the host machine. This card, when inserted into a Nuclear Control Industrial Information Panel, will receive runtime information transmitted by the host machine, including its current location. Additionally, it returns the same information that its lower-tech sibling, the GregTech Sensor Kit, provides. Unlike the GregTech Sensor Kit, the Metrics Transmitter Cover §nworks interdimensionally and at any range without the need of range upgrades.§r In addition, since covers remain on machines when they are dismantled, the paired sensor card §nwill continue to work even if the host machine is relocated, and never needs to be recalibrated.§r This makes it perfect for the Ore Drilling Plant and Oil/Gas/Fluid Drilling Rig, which are deployed in the field and often have to be relocated.%n%nHowever, like always, there's a catch. If the Metrics Transmitter Cover is detached from its host machine, §nthe paired sensor card will be destroyed.§r Maybe you shouldn't be using a crowbar around sensitive electronics...
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAKyg.desc=This produces power out of Rocket Fuels. To see how to make them, look at the Space Race tab. These are specifically GT++ Rocket Fuels, and automating them for powergen in this multi will also provide you with endless fuel for your space travels.%n%nThe math regarding the Rocketdyne is complicated. Looking at the controller's tooltip helps, but the main gist of it is like this: provide Carbon Dioxide and make sure it doesn't run out, choose the EU/t you want to get, calculate the amount of fuel you need for the fuel you will use, and then provide enough Liquid Hydrogen to boost the multi, according to the EU/t value.%n%nYou will always want to have the Rocketdyne boosted, for several reasons. Assuming you have at least an IV 4A Dynamo Hatch, outputting close to the maximum on that hatch will lower the fuel efficiency, but not if it's boosted. Additionally, this multi doesn't consume fuel continuously, but with intervals of 1 second between consuming and not consuming, while generating power all the same. Boosting this consumption results in huge fuel efficiency, combined with the high fuel values of the Rocket Fuels.%n%n[warn]Beware, letting the dynamo overfill can lead to an explosion! Be sure you have a place to output the energy.[/warn]
betterquesting.quest.EOlpI83vT36jaFwDH7pS7w.desc=To insert and extract many amps from your LSC, make these special hatches.%n%nAll multiblocks that accept regular Dynamo Hatches also accept 4A Dynamo Hatches.%n%nSome multiblocks, like the LSC, support multi-amp hatches above 4A and laser hatches.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAL0w.desc=The Dangote Distillus is not enough for the goals of an oil baron. You might have heard about "mega" multiblocks, namely the Mega EBF, but did you know that a Distillation Tower equivalent exists?%n%nLike the Dangote, it processes recipes in parallel, but it can handle 256 at a time and is much, much bigger than anything you've built so far. My challenge to you is to build a max-height, full-sized Mega Distillation Tower!
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAL1Q.desc=This is the most powerful combustion engine that has ever been built. In fact, it's not only that, but also a Gas Turbine and a Rocket Fuel Generator!%n%nThe Universal Chemical Fuel Engine burns fuel with some additives, as did its predecessors, but it runs at a lower efficiency. The 150%% value is a mathematical limit, you cannot reach it without supplying infinite fuel, but this engine compensates by running as fast as fuel is input into it, without the maximum EU/t limitation the others had. The only two things you have to make sure of are that you supply enough Combustion Promoter to keep efficiency up (I'll let you figure the best ratio on your own, but 1:4 promoter:fuel is decent), and that the dynamo can support the EU/t that the generator is outputting.%n%n
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAALrg.desc=Welcome to EV! If you thought the previous tier had a big jump in oil processing, you are correct, but now it's going to jump up all over again!%n%nThis tier does not unlock new processing multis like HV did, but it does bring better, much better generators. From now on, your main generator options will almost always be multiblocks, unless you need an easy-to-move generator for a multiblock miner or something similar. For your diesel fuels, the next step is the Large Combustion Engine (LCE), and there is a quest for it on the Multiblock Goals tab as usual. This, however, is a big investment in Titanium, amongst other things, so I hope you have that processing automated already.%n%nIf you boost the LCE, you will get a huge boost in both EU/t and efficiency. While an HV Diesel Generator had an output of 512 EU/t at 85%% efficiency, this expensive multi outputs 6144 EU/t at 150%% efficiency! Make sure you have an EV 4A Dynamo Hatch that can handle this output.%nThere is an equivalent turbine for gases, like the Refinery Gas you might be using to power your oil processing setup, which is cheaper to build but its performance depends on the turbine placed inside it, and you won't be able to get near the levels of the LCE unless you get some Tungstensteel and a good metal like Shadow Metal.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAALxA.desc=Have you built an Oil Cracker? Have you checked its coils? This multi gets a significant discount to EU/t when upgrading the coils, but the discount caps at 50%% with HSS-G coils. If you are still using low-tier coils, this is a great time to upgrade them to TPV and enjoy a 40%% discount. Nichrome coils offer a 30%% discount.%n%nBy the way, you can wall-share Oil Crackers, just like DTs, LCRs and many other multis, and doing this will save on the amount of coils you need!%n%n[note]You only need to make one of the three coil types.[/note]
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAALzg.desc=Very similar to the LCE in most aspects, the Extreme Combustion Engine was created to close the gap between the diesels and more advanced forms of powergen, mainly nuclear fusion. However, the main thing they differ on is the fuel that they can run, and in this case you're limited to the powerful fuel from the last tier, High Octane Gasoline.%n%nThat's right, only this fuel will work, and in exchange the ECE will output more than 10k EU/t. If you add Liquid Oxygen, which you'll need 4 Vacuum Freezers for (3 at HV and 1 at EV), you can keep it boosted permanently, which will send it up to 4 IV amps of power and 150%% fuel efficiency. It's in your best interest to keep this thing going if you want to keep using Oil fuels for power, and the only thing you can rely on is your automated HOG setup, which you might have to, and should improve with the new IV multis as soon as you can, unless you have other sources of power working simultaneously.%n%nAs a last note, there is also an IV equivalent of the Vacuum Freezer, if you want to tackle the Liquid Oxygen needs that way. It's more power efficient, look it up on the Mass Processing tab.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMQA.desc=If you've gotten this far, you should be ready to produce Steam at an alarming rate from this hyper-efficient fuel. Unlike Combustion Generators and Gas Turbines, you will need more multis in front of your Large Boiler because it outputs Superheated Steam. More specifically, you will need two turbines: one for turning the Superheated Steam into EU and regular Steam, and another for turning the regular Steam into EU and water, to be reused in the boiler.%n%nThe multis will not run without a turbine inside the controller. The size and material of a turbine determines the optimal flow rate and the EU/t at that rate. Good materials in EV are Shadow Metal (from Thaumcraft) and Manyullyn, before upgrading to Oriharukon in IV. Steam turbines usually generate less EU/t than gas turbines but that depends on the amount and tier of the boilers, and whether you are using loose mode or not (check the Steam Turbine quest for more details).%n%nSteam flow rates are very high which means you will need huge GT pipes to keep up, but there is a better way: AE2 P2P tunnels, set to fluid mode, can teleport fluids from one multi to the next without caring for high flow rates. With all that taken care of, the only thing left to do is place an EV 4A Dynamo Hatch on each turbine. Now your setup is complete!
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMVw.desc=What a complicated name this is. What does it mean?%n%nWell, it's what is called a molten salt reactor. The Liquid Fluoride part means that the nuclear fuel is actually a liquid, mixed in with fluoride salts. This is a mechanism that makes it more difficult to get the fuel ready for fission, but also makes the process more efficient, gives out more byproducts and also removes the danger of explosion. That's right, nuclear meltdowns are a thing of the past! The molten salt is designed to flow downwards into a hole where it solidifies, in case the reactor has problems, so it's impossible for the fission process to continue into an explosive mess.%n%nThere are three downsides, though. One of them was mentioned just above, the fuel needs more processing to be ready for the LFTR, and more input materials to reach the right mixture. After it goes through the reactor, it comes out as depleted, and this part too requires more processing steps, although it gives out a lot more useful chemicals than the single Lutetium/Plutonium the IC2 nuke depletion process gave. Lastly, the molten salt is very hot and very corrosive, which means it would destroy the materials used to build the IC2 nukes. You will need newer, stronger and more expensive materials to build a reactor, not to mention its much larger size.%n%nThe structure for this multi is truly something else. It has not one, but four required 4A Dynamo Hatches, either EV, IV or LuV depending on the fuel being fed into the reactor, with better fuels being unlocked at later progression stages. This means that one LFTR makes either 1 LuV amp, 1 ZPM amp or 1 UV amp while running. It also requires 4 Muffler Hatches, when it has no pollution output!%n%nOther than this, all the inputs and outputs are fluids. The minimum amount you'll need is 2 inputs and 4 outputs, although one of the outputs comes out over time, and not on recipe finish. This output is Uranium 233, a very rare isotope that can get you deeper into LFTR fuels and more power, hardly obtainable from any other source.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMew.desc=Whether you've mathed it out from NEI, looked at the spreadsheet or done something else, you might have figured something out: Fuel 3 is better in every way. More power, more byproducts, more everything. However, both recipes for it use Thorium Tetrafluoride (TF4), and the source of this is salt sparging, done in the Sparge Tower. Not only that, but Fuel 3 can only be consumed by having 4 LuV 4A Dynamo Hatches in the LFTR, which means that it's a fair bit away from the previous steps in this chain.%n%nOnce you've made it there, though, you can start working on getting this fuel. To make it, you will need at least one Sparge Tower dedicated to using Fluorine, with T Salt or TB Salt (TB Salt is better, get it from Fuel 2). There is a recipe that uses Helium, but it's not required for Fuel 3 and is meant for byproducts, so the quest for it is in the breeding half of this branch. Using a single tower for both recipes is a bad idea, so don't do it!%n%nPreferably, you should input Fluorine and TB Salt and let it run for a while. Speeding up the recipe by overclocking and making more towers is a good idea, since the TF4 is your bottleneck now. Alongside it, you get several fluorides: Lithium, Neptunium, Technetium and Selenium. These might prove useful in the future, but your goal is the Thorium one.
betterquesting.quest.AAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAMwA.desc=Some flowers eat bees. Some eat leaves. Some eat slimes. This one eats everything (everything you can eat, anyway). The Gourmaryllis is happiest when provided with delicious meals, so I hope the HV-tier diet of canned sludge hasn't made you forget how to cook.
betterquesting.quest.TL8RVz_HTBO5LvkI6SQi6A.desc=In order to obtain more exotic particles than simple protons, neutrons, and electrons, you will need the Large Hadron Collider. You can use any charged particle as input, sourced from any other beam-like multiblock such as the Source Chamber.%n%nThe LHC's four modules can each produce a different set of particles. For a particle to become eligible for output, the §bCollision Energy§r must be at least the particle's §dRest Mass§r, shown on its tooltip in NEI. Particles with a §dRest Mass§r below 0.5 MeV still require at least 0.5 MeV of §bCollision Energy§r.%n%nThe LHC has two modes: §lAccelerator§r and §lCollider§r.%n%nFirst, in §lAccelerator§r mode, it accelerates the input beam to a higher energy. It does this in 1-second cycles, with more energy added per cycle as the §9Number of Completed Cycles§r increases. The power draw increases quadratically as the §9Number of Completed Cycles§r increases, and linearly as the §cAmount§r increases.%n%nYou can set a target §6Beam Energy§r and a maximum §9Number of Cycles§r in the UI. The beam itself is capped at 1 TeV, so keep the target at or below 1 TeV. Setting a higher target prevents the §cAmount§r from growing. If your beam reaches the target §6Beam Energy§r before reaching the maximum cycle count, further completed cycles increase the beam's §cAmount§r instead, which also increases your power draw. Below 15,000, each of these cycles multiplies the §cAmount§r by 1.3, rounded up. At or above 15,000, each cycle instead adds (0.3 × current Amount)^0.5, rounded up. Once the maximum §9Number of Cycles§r is reached, the LHC automatically switches to §lCollider§r mode.%n%nLater on, you can improve this scaling by supplying a Booster Fluid through an Input Hatch and selecting it under §lBeam Booster§r in the UI. Degenerate Quark-Gluon Plasma raises the exponent in the formula from 0.5 to 0.7, while Molten Magmatter raises it to 0.9. This lets you reach much higher §cAmounts§r with additional cycles.%n%nUsing either Booster Fluid immediately sets the §6Beam Energy§r to 1 TeV. As long as your target is at or below 1 TeV, the acceleration cycles can increase the §cAmount§r right from the start. The LHC consumes 1L of fluid per current §cAmount§r every second, in both §lAccelerator§r and §lCollider§r modes. For example, an §cAmount§r of 20,000 requires 20,000 L/s. As the §cAmount§r grows, so does the fluid consumption. If there is not enough fluid for the next cycle, the machine shuts down.%n%nChanging the §lBeam Booster§r setting requires restarting the machine and accelerating a new beam from scratch. You can also select Booster Fluids in the built in calculator to see how they affect the final beam and power draw before committing to a run.%n%n%nIn §lCollider§r mode, the beam is collided with itself to generate all kinds of particles. Each LHC Module is able to detect and capture a certain subset of particles, depending on which Fundamental Force the particle can interact with. This also means some particles appear in multiple modules. You can blacklist particles from appearing by using the Filtered Beamline Output Hatch.%n%n§l[note]§lThe §b§lCollision Energy§r §lis 2x the accelerated §6§lBeam Energy§r§l, up to a maximum of 2 TeV.§r[/note]
betterquesting.quest.XKKP2E5ORG-ju42dSDd3sw.desc=In order to compress singularities and eventually infinity catalysts, you'll need the strongest compressor yet: the Neutronium Compressor. This multiblock channels and controls extreme amounts of pressure through carefully calibrated Active Neutronium Compressor Casings, but the sheer magnitude of pressure is too much to produce blocks or superdense plates, as any regular material inserted into the device will be compressed down to a singularity. More advanced singularities should be possible in theory, but you'll need something even stronger...%n%n[note]Note that singularity recipes require extreme amounts of items! Consider using Compressed Buses, Quantum Buses, or ME Stocking Input Buses to fit everything in there.[/note]
